    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93319" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαρδόνυξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠχος</span>,
			ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάρδιον</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sardonyx</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philem.
				216
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				5.46
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				1.116
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				3.7.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BJ</u>
				5.5.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Apoc.</u>
				21.20
			</span></i>, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Fluv.</u>
				20.4
			</span></i>, etc. The stone was called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνυξ</span> when the dark ground was simply spotted or
			streaked with white, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαρδόνυξ</span>
			if the different colours were disposed in layers.</div>
